// RtOp, text: Text, numbers, regular expressions, panics, `std.base64` and `std.compress`. Read by `compiler/kir/build.rs`.
StrLen,
StrIsEmpty,
StrUpper,
StrLower,
StrTrim,
StrContains,
StrStartsWith,
StrEndsWith,
StrRepeat,
WrappingAdd,
WrappingSub,
WrappingMul,
CheckedAdd,
CheckedSub,
CheckedMul,
CheckedDiv,
/// Whether `a` and `b` (`Int`s) added (`c` 0), subtracted (1) or
/// multiplied (2) fit in an `Int` (`compiler/kir/src/checked_fits.rs`).
CheckedFits,
/// More methods of text and lists (spec 14.2).
StrReplace,
StrLines,
StrChars,
StrIndexOf,
StrSlice,
MathSqrt,
MathPow,
MathFloor,
MathCeil,
MathRound,
/// `math.sin` and the other angle functions, `exp` and `ln` (spec 14.5),
/// on `Float`s; `MathAtan2` takes `y`, then `x`.
MathSin,
MathCos,
MathTan,
MathAsin,
MathAcos,
MathAtan,
MathAtan2,
MathExp,
MathLn,
/// `math.log10`, `cbrt`, `hypot`, `remainder`, `erfc` and `lgamma` (spec
/// 14.5) on `Float`s; `hypot` and `remainder` take `x`, then `y`.
MathLog10,
MathCbrt,
MathHypot,
MathRemainder,
MathErfc,
MathLgamma,
/// `std.regex` (spec 14.8). Compiling can fail.
RegexNew,
RegexAdvanced,
RegexIsMatch,
RegexFind,
RegexFindAll,
RegexCaptures,
RegexNamedCaptures,
RegexReplace,
RegexReplaceAll,
RegexSplit,
StrSplit,
StrBytes,
/// A `Float`'s IEEE 754 bits and back (spec 14.2): the slot already
/// holds them, so the runtime gives its operand back.
FloatBits,
FloatFromBits,
/// `panic(message)` with a message computed while the program runs
/// (spec 5.6); a written-out message is `ExprKind::Panic`.
PanicText,
/// `a ** b` for whole numbers of the result's type (spec 1.8): panics
/// when `b` is negative or the result doesn't fit.
IntPow,
/// `a.near(b)` on floats (spec 14.2).
FloatNear,
/// `d.round(places)` (`c` is 0) and `d.round_even(places)` (`c` is 1)
/// on a `Decimal` (spec 14.2).
DecRound,
/// `match` on an `Error` (spec 5.5): the error it holds, past any
/// `context`, as the optional of the result's type: `none` when it is
/// of another type.
ErrorAs,
/// `std.base64` (spec 14.20): `encode` (data, URL-safe, padded) and
/// `decode` (text, URL-safe), which can fail.
Base64Encode,
Base64Decode,
/// `std.text`'s normal forms (spec 14.9): the text and the form (0 NFC,
/// 1 NFD, 2 NFKC, 3 NFKD), from an entry of its own.
NormalizeText,
/// `std.compress` (spec 14.21): `encode_bytes` (data, format, level) and
/// `decode_bytes` (data, format, most), which can fail.
CompressEncode,
CompressDecode,
/// Text methods (spec 14.2, `runtime/native/src/rt_text_methods.rs`),
/// on the text in `a` (owned): `b` a `String` (owned) or an `Int`, and
/// for padding `c` the fill `Char`.
TextTrimStart,
TextTrimEnd,
TextCapitalize,
TextTitle,
TextIsBlank,
TextWords,
TextLastIndexOf,
TextCount,
TextRemovePrefix,
TextRemoveSuffix,
TextPadLeft,
TextPadRight,
/// A `Char`'s kind check (spec 14.2, *Characters*): the character's
/// code point in `a`, and in `b` the check's place in
/// `kavach_runtime_core::text_methods::CHAR_CHECKS`.
TextCharIs,
/// `s[a:b:step]` (spec 2.19): the text, and a list of the slice's four
/// words, as `ListSlicePart`; by characters.
StrSlicePart,
/// `s[i]`: character `i` of the text; panics when out of range.
StrAt,
/// Arithmetic and checks on a whole-number type with its own limits
/// (`Int<bits: 24>`, `Int<range: 1..=9>`, spec 2.1): `c` is the place
/// of the op in `WHOLE_OPS`, shifted left 32 bits, joined with the code
/// of the type's `Shape::Whole` (or of `Int8` … `UInt64`). Panics as
/// the interpreter does when a result doesn't fit.
IntWhole,
/// `s[a:b]`, `s[a:]` and `s[:b]` (spec 2.19) with no step and no `#`:
/// the text, the start (0 when not written) and the end (the largest
/// `Int` when not written), with no list of words (Sakshi's S8).
StrSliceRange,
